<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grebo people</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Grebo are a Kru-speaking people of south-eastern Liberia and neighbouring south-western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-coast">Côte d'Ivoire</a>, living around <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cape-palmas">Cape Palmas</a>, along the coast and in the Cavalla River valley. Many Grebo worked as sailors and labourers on European ships. They clashed repeatedly with the Americo-Liberian settlers of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maryland">Maryland</a> and Liberia over land and trade, notably in the war of 1856–1857 and in later risings in 1875 and 1910.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grebo-people.jpg" alt="Grebo people" width="320" height="203" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Couple_Grebo-1906.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
